Temp-table anchor: CREATE TEMP TABLE + INSERT seeds + ONE walk statement (SQLite, through the backend's session)
    [wall-clock side note] temp table create+insert+walk+drop: 0.15s
    statements=4 (BEGIN, CREATE, INSERT, WITH, DROP); rows returned=12003; == chunked CTE: True
    [NOT RUN: other engines] Postgres/MariaDB: CREATE TEMPORARY TABLE is per-session, one DDL + bulk INSERT; SQL Server: #temp tables likewise; Oracle: DDL commits the transaction and global temporary tables must be pre-created (18c+ private temp tables ORA$PTT_ exist). The seeds still cost one bind each on the INSERT, chunked by the bind budget, so the statement count is 1 + ceil(S / budget) + 1, never fewer than the IN-list form.

